        "story": {
          "success": {
            "en": "“कुर्वन्ति,” you say, and every spirit in the circle drops its hands from its ears. A hush, and then a sound like a great number of very small tools being laid down at once: they have heard, they are doing. Drawers five and eight shut, one after the other, with the softest clicks of all.",
